\section{Parameter scales and intervals}{

\itemize{
\item Regression coefficients are reported on the model's coefficient scale.
\item SDs are positive natural SDs; intervals are constructed on the log scale
and transformed back. Testing an SD against zero is a boundary problem,
so summaries do not supply a usual zero-test p-value for SDs.
\item Correlations are reported between -1 and 1; intervals and summary tests
use the Fisher (\code{atanh}) scale and transform interval limits back.
\item Fixed parameters remain in \code{coef()} and have zero covariance rows/columns.
Their inferential entries, including confidence limits, are \code{NA}.
}

These are Wald intervals. Stored optimizer-coordinate covariance is used when
available; supplied matrices and older fits without it use the natural-scale
delta method. Numerical convergence alone does not establish interval coverage.
}

